# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# brahma-web — environment variables
#
# HOW TO USE (Windows PowerShell, in the project folder):
#   Copy-Item .env.example .env.local
#   notepad .env.local
# Fill in the blanks, then File → Save. Notepad saves as UTF-8, which is what
# Next.js needs. Do NOT create this file with `echo ... > .env.local` in
# PowerShell — that writes UTF-16 and Next.js cannot read it.
#
# .env.local is git-ignored: it never gets committed or pushed.
#
# WHERE EACH VALUE GOES
#   Name                                   .env.local   Vercel
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL               yes          yes
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY   yes          yes
#   CRON_SECRET                            optional     yes
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL                   no           yes (once the domain is live)
#   SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY                    yes          NEVER
#   GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY                    if enriching NEVER
#
# After changing anything on Vercel, redeploy — variables are read at build.
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════


# ── 1. Supabase project URL ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Already correct for the "BRAHMAS Website" project.
# Where it comes from: supabase.com → project → Project Settings → Data API
# → "Project URL".
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://dynxjlgdoftzgfsuezwc.supabase.co


# ── 2. Supabase publishable key ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Already correct. PUBLIC by design — row-level security only lets it read
# published content, so it is safe in the browser and in this file.
# Where it comes from: Project Settings → API Keys → "Publishable key"
# (starts with sb_publishable_).
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=sb_publishable_gmUzBErZDiOwO0mql6sPlg_DlWzzPIE


# ── 3. Keep-alive secret ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Any long random string. Vercel's daily cron sends it to /api/keepalive so the
# free Supabase project never pauses after a quiet week. Make one with:
#   node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"
# Paste the SAME value into Vercel. Locally it is only needed to test the route.
CRON_SECRET=


# ── 4. Public site address ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The final https address, no trailing slash — e.g. https://www.example.com
# Used for share previews (WhatsApp/LinkedIn cards) and canonical links.
# Leave empty locally. On Vercel, add it once the custom domain is connected;
# until then Vercel's own address is used automatically.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=


# ── 5. Supabase SECRET key — LOCAL ONLY ─────────────────────────────────────
# Only used by `npm run editor` (scripts/editors.mjs) to create / remove admin
# logins from YOUR computer. It bypasses all security rules, so:
#   - NEVER put it on Vercel, and never rename it with a NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix;
#   - never paste it into chat, email, or a commit.
# Where it comes from: Project Settings → API Keys → "Secret keys" → copy
# (starts with sb_secret_). If it is ever exposed, delete it there and make a
# new one.
SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY=


# ── 6. Google Places key — LOCAL ONLY, optional ─────────────────────────────
# Only for `npm run enrich` (scripts/enrich-properties.mjs). The website never
# reads it. Where it comes from: console.cloud.google.com → APIs & Services →
# Credentials. Keep it secret; never on Vercel.
GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=
